        -1040,
        -864
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 1080,
        "content": "## Payment Reconciliation Engine - Matching, Exceptions & Audit\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs on a schedule (or manual test trigger), pulls incoming payment transactions from a bank/PSP feed and open invoices/orders from your accounting or ERP system, and runs a deterministic matching engine against them. Each payment is classified as matched (exact reference + amount), partial (within tolerance or needs a human pick between candidates), or unmatched. Matched payments are auto-applied to the ledger; partial matches go to Slack for human review with an approve/reject decision; unmatched payments are logged as exceptions and flagged to finance. Every outcome is written to an audit log, and a run summary is posted to Slack at the end.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect your bank/PSP API credentials (or file/SFTP source) to 'Fetch Payment Transactions'.\n- Connect your accounting/ERP API credentials to 'Fetch Open Invoices' and to the ledger update calls ('Update Invoice as Paid', 'Apply Manual Match').\n- Connect Google Sheets (or your database of choice) credentials for the audit log and exceptions log.\n- Connect Slack credentials for review requests, exception alerts, and the run summary.\n- Configure the Set Configuration Parameters node: amount tolerance, date tolerance, currency, API base URLs, sheet IDs, and Slack channels.\n- Review the matching logic in 'Reconciliation Matching Engine' to match your reference-number conventions and business rules before enabling production use.\n- Set the schedule interval on 'Run on Schedule' to match how often your payment feed updates.\n\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
